# P05R-T08: normalize text line endings.
# The execution packet and execution notes carry byte-integrity checks
# (SHA256SUMS.txt + tools/validate_packet.py). With core.autocrlf=true and no
# attributes, a fresh Windows clone checks those files out as CRLF and the
# validator reports FAIL against the LF-committed hashes. Pinning eol=lf for
# both trees makes checkouts byte-stable on every OS.
* text=auto
LoreForge_Execution_Packet/** text eol=lf
execution-notes/** text eol=lf
# Archives must never pass through text filters (rule order: this wins over
# the packet eol rule above). A zip whose header bytes contain no NUL can be
# misdetected as text and corrupted by CRLF normalization otherwise. The
# `binary` macro does not reset eol, so eol is explicitly unset too.
*.zip binary -eol
